## PASTE C — MAGIC-CHAT LANDING ART ENHANCEMENT

The OBI landing overlay currently shows: pulsing OBI title + 3 mode cards with art arsenal icons. Add one of the gemini concept art pieces as a full-bleed background to the landing overlay, tinted dark so text stays readable.

**In magic-chat.html CSS** — find the `.landing-overlay` rule and add background:

```css
.landing-overlay {
    /* existing properties stay */
    background-image: url('https://net-art-arsenal.pages.dev/thumbs/artwork/gemini-concept-art-07.webp');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
}
/* Ensure the dark overlay still reads — add ::before tint if not already there */
.landing-overlay::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(10, 10, 18, 0.82);
    z-index: 0;
}
.landing-overlay > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
```

*Use gemini-concept-art-07 (or whichever you know looks best — swap the number). The thumbs WebP keeps load fast on mobile.*

**Additionally:** The OBI header area in the main chat UI (after landing dismissed) has the lion avatar. Add `NET-PHXRISING-LOGO.webp` as a faint watermark behind the chat window itself:

Find `<main id="chatMain"` or the main content wrapper and add inline style:
```html
style="position:relative;"
```
Then inside it, add as first child:
```html
<div style="position:fixed;bottom:60px;right:16px;opacity:0.04;width:200px;height:200px;pointer-events:none;z-index:0;background:url('/assessment-assets/brand/NET-PHXRISING-LOGO.webp') center/contain no-repeat;" aria-hidden="true"></div>
```

